<!-- order-delivered — the order arrived (053 US3).

     ⚠ THE ONLY MESSAGE A WEB-ONLY SHOPPER GETS ABOUT THEIR DELIVERY. Until 053 the three
     post-payment lifecycle events (ready, out for delivery, delivered) were PUSH ONLY, so a customer
     who shops on the website and never installed the app heard nothing after the receipt.

     ⚠ IT NAMES NO SHOP AND NO PACKAGE COUNT (FR-021). Effy's fulfilment nodes are hidden by the
     product model: a customer buys from one brand and never learns which shops served them, nor how
     many. "Your 2 parcels have arrived" is the single easiest way to leak that, which is why the
     catalogue entry gives this template no `items` var to make the mistake with.

     ⚠ IT DOES NOT RESTATE THE RECEIPT. That document was sent at payment and does a different job.
     Repeating the total here would invite the reader to reconcile two documents that were produced at
     different moments — and would put an amount in a message whose subject is arrival.

     ⚠ NO CONDITION CLAIM. The platform knows a package was handed over and that someone recorded it
     arriving. It does not know the contents were correct or undamaged, so nothing here says so — and
     the help line below is the honest counterweight. -->

<mjml lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <mj-head>
    <mj-include path="../generated/theme.mjml" />
    <mj-title>Your {{effyProductName}} order {{orderNumber}} has arrived</mj-title>
    <mj-preview>Everything in your order has been delivered.</mj-preview>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body width="600px" background-color="#f5f5f5" css-class="e-bg-page">
    <mj-include path="../components/header.mjml" />

    <mj-section padding="0 32px 32px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text mj-class="h1" css-class="e-ink e-h1">
          Your order has arrived
        </mj-text>

        <mj-text mj-class="muted" css-class="e-muted" padding="12px 0 0 0">
          Order {{orderNumber}} was delivered on {{deliveredOn}}. Thanks for shopping with
          {{effyProductName}}.
        </mj-text>

        <!-- Both dark classes named so the label inverts with the fill — 038 shipped a receipt button
             that was invisible in dark mode because the class landed on the wrapping <td> while the
             colour sat on an inner element. -->
        <mj-button href="{{orderUrl}}" css-class="e-btn-bg e-btn-fg" align="left" padding="24px 0 0 0">
          View your order
        </mj-button>

        <!-- ⚠ The counterweight to a message that asserts a delivery nobody at Effy witnessed. With
             no carrier integration, "arrived" is recorded by a person; if it did not arrive, the
             customer needs somewhere to say so, and it must not read as an apology in advance. -->
        <mj-text mj-class="small" css-class="e-muted" padding="20px 0 0 0">
          Something not right? Reply to this email or write to {{effySupportEmail}} and we&rsquo;ll
          sort it out.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-include path="../components/footer.mjml" />
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
